                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ddb56801-2adf-32cc-bea2-2e5b3c86abc5",
                        "entry_id": "8ba78753-adc4-3d71-b310-19ba6fbb5a0e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A gun or cannon, especially a rifle, as seen from the imagined perspective of an uncivilized person or an animal."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "05707c58-03a0-4afb-ae47-4fc468341182",
                                "sense_id": "ddb56801-2adf-32cc-bea2-2e5b3c86abc5",
                                "text": "The man pointed his thunderstick at the buffalo, and with a great noise and fire, the buffalo fell down dead."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6757791e-f37e-4391-adf9-397ac3142788",
                                "sense_id": "ddb56801-2adf-32cc-bea2-2e5b3c86abc5",
                                "text": "We sneaked into the soldiers' camp, and stole five thundersticks."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "72430ac4-85ae-4739-9d1f-08d0fdff2862",
                                "sense_id": "ddb56801-2adf-32cc-bea2-2e5b3c86abc5",
                                "text": "...the Men, when they hunt us with their arrows or a thunder-stick which strikes with a loud noise..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab7bf18c-4b2e-4bfe-bec2-cd36aad19788",
                                "sense_id": "ddb56801-2adf-32cc-bea2-2e5b3c86abc5",
                                "text": "Two men with beards... carrying thundersticks... were in the village above..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "040977cb-f8bf-4d65-b666-9473352dbd72",
                                "sense_id": "ddb56801-2adf-32cc-bea2-2e5b3c86abc5",
                                "text": "We have heard that they have magic thunder sticks; that all they need do is point the stick at a man and thunder and lightning comes out of it and the man dies."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3002be00-0474-41e1-b115-315525063ff4",
                                "sense_id": "ddb56801-2adf-32cc-bea2-2e5b3c86abc5",
                                "text": "(Two bears discussing a rifle found lying on the ground): Thunderstick? ...You actually said 'Thunderstick?'... That, my friend, is a Winchester 30.06."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd469843-bd49-4cdb-9ac3-229bd260066d",
                                "sense_id": "ddb56801-2adf-32cc-bea2-2e5b3c86abc5",
                                "text": "...the captain of the vessel ordered a crew member to fire the thunderstick, as ancestors called the gun.\nWord of bearded White men and their thundersticks was carried inland to other Indians."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6d2db992-e4f3-3dfb-ad44-4233778e5a05",
                        "entry_id": "8ba78753-adc4-3d71-b310-19ba6fbb5a0e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A narrow plastic balloon that is used as a promotional noise maker by hitting one against another."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1b635edc-8a31-4e5b-9a59-018af6c1b2e8",
                                "sense_id": "6d2db992-e4f3-3dfb-ad44-4233778e5a05",
                                "text": "Called “James Tenney and Milton Babbitt : American Iconoclasts,” the mini-festival begins on Saturday with a work by Mr. Tenney, who died in 2006, on a program including pieces by Larry Polansky, Michael Byron and Henry Cowell (the 1925 “Ensemble” for string quartet and thundersticks). Mr. Babbitt is honored on Sunday with a program that includes, among other works, a premiere by Christopher Buchenholz."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
